    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our premier offensive anchor. His score of 80.40 against Kirby is the highest in the lineup, buoyed by a significant +16% park factor and a robust dynamic platoon advantage. Alongside him, **Jackson Merrill** (74.39) is our most efficient play; his favorable matchup against Singer, combined with an elite +13% platoon boost, makes him a primary source of run production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.17) and **Kyle Tucker** (64.59) remain essential starts despite challenging matchups against Luzardo and Jones, as their inherent talent floors continue to outweigh the moderate skill of their opposing starters.\n\nPlatoon edges are dictating much of our middle-to-lower order, particularly with **Nasim Nunez** (58.52) and **Wade Meckler** (57.50). **Nasim Nunez** utilizes his switch-hitting profile to mitigate Ray's effectiveness, while **Wade Meckler** benefits from a strong +12% SP skill rating and positive park factors. The tightest decision on the bench was **Miguel Vargas**, who posted a 42.35 efficiency score. While **Miguel Vargas** remains a viable depth option, the combination of a daunting matchup against the elite Sale (2.97 xERA) and superior positional output from our active utility spots kept him on the pine.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the bottom of the order, specifically **Brayan Rocchio** (49.10) and **Dominic Smith** (49.28). Both are hovering near the marginal tier and rely heavily on the hope that Rod\u00f3n and Martin experience command issues. While **Liam Hicks** (58.72) is currently projected to start, his efficiency is highly dependent on his lead-off spot; we are monitoring the lineup for any late-breaking adjustments. No severe weather flags are present, but the high xERA of Ray suggests our infielders\u2014**Curtis Mead** included\u2014may see more scoring opportunities than the raw projections currently suggest.",
